think Read the cohort at the head of the lap, as every lap of this arc does. Hashing all forty-four bodies returned exactly one hash, so for the first time in the arc there was no outlier to read and no rung staying home.
think Lifted the body into caravan/ladder_checks.rye as pub fn confirm_pruned(comptime rung: type, io: std.Io, domain: []const u8, count: u32) bool, prefixing max_confirm_looks, read_count, and note_rest_ms with rung. The std.Io.sleep call and both bound asserts stay exactly as the forty-four wrote them.
think Rewrote all forty-four rungs to three-line stubs with an awk pass excluding caravan/ladder_checks.rye by name, and confirmed each stubbed rung already imports ladder_checks. The loop reported forty-four, matching REACH_OK.
think Lowered the carry ceiling from 71898 to 71382, repointed the two measured asserts, and rewrote the fold-queue and GREEN prose with numbers spelled as words, since caravan_ladder_prose_count_scan.sh refuses a bare digit run no assert holds.
